<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Shaoxing</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1141</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jin-song-wars">Jin–Song wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaoxing">Shaoxing</a> of 1141 ended the wars between the Southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-jin-dynasty">Jurchen Jin dynasty</a>. It fixed the frontier along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huai-river">Huai River</a>, made the Song emperor a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the Jin and obliged the Song to pay an annual tribute of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>. It was arranged by the chief minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> Hui, and the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yue-fei">Yue Fei</a>, who opposed the peace, was executed.</p></div>
